@startuml
title sd - Locate a concept and open its exercise
actor Learner
participant "Course in browser" as Course
participant "Static host" as Host
participant "GitHub practice repository" as GitHub
participant "Local IDE and toolchain" as IDE
Learner -> Course : open course
Course -> Host : request page and static assets
Host --> Course : course map, navigation, local search
Learner -> Course : find concept by module ID or keyword
Course -> Course : search loaded browser index
Course --> Learner : matching modules and availability
Learner -> Course : open selected module
Course -> Host : request module content
Host --> Course : published lesson or planned status
alt lesson and exercise available
  Course --> Learner : explanation, UML, verified GitHub link
  Learner -> GitHub : follow exact exercise/revision link
  GitHub --> Learner : matching source and clone instructions
  Learner -> IDE : clone repository, open matching exercise
  IDE -> GitHub : git clone / checkout accepted revision
  GitHub --> IDE : source, design, tests, build instructions
  Learner -> IDE : implement, compile and test locally
else lesson or exercise not yet published
  Course --> Learner : explicit availability, no nonexistent target link
end
@enduml
